-- title:
--   Local box at ̄ r of the centraliser order
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ and $\bar r$ be primes with $\bar r \neq r$. Let $a,b \in \mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring (every nonzero element is a unit) precisely when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$. Let $\Lambda \subseteq \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule that is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and every order containing it equals it. Let $c,d \in \mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt c d r` ($c<0$, $d<0$, and $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring exactly for the $v$ containing $r$), with $O$ a maximal order in it, and let $a_1,b_1 \in \mathbb{Q}$ satisfy the corresponding condition at $\bar r$. Let $j : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \to M_2(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d])$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map carrying $\Lambda$ into matrices with all entries in $O$, and let $\tau : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_2(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d])$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map whose image is exactly the set of matrices commuting with every $j(m)$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ consisting exactly of those $x$ all of whose matrix entries $\tau(x)_{il}$ lie in $O$, let $\Lambda_1$ be any maximal order in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$, and let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $\bar r$. Then the local boxes of $R$ and of $\Lambda_1$ at $w$ coincide, where the local box of a submodule $M$ at $w$ is the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in M$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_w$.
--
--   This is the local step identifying, at the place $w$ above $\bar r$, the completion of the centraliser order $\tau^{-1}(M_2(O))$ with that of an arbitrary maximal order of the definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $\bar r$; since both completions are the unique maximal order of the local division algebra, they agree. It is used by [`QuaternionAlgebra.exists_units_forall_mem_localBox_iff_of_forall_iff_mem_range_of_isMaximalOrder`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.exists_units_forall_mem_localBox_iff_of_forall_iff_mem_range_of_isMaximalOrder) in the quaternionic interchange of invariants underlying the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the relevant Shimura curves.
-- source:
